{"id": "EUVD-2026-104588", "enisaUuid": "93baa346-44fa-3fcc-98c9-3ededb75cfbc", "description": "Grav 1.7.53 before 1.7.53.5 and 2.0.0-rc.8 before 2.2.2 contains a resource exhaustion vulnerability that allows anonymous visitors to bypass the system.images.max_pixels limit when system.images.url_actions is enabled. Attackers can send single-dimension or percentage forceResize, zoomCrop, or chained image actions to make GD allocate multi-gigabyte canvases, exhausting server memory and taking the site down.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T19:10:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T16:09:47", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/getgrav/grav/security/advisories/GHSA-8gr9-59p6-r488", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/grav-before-1.7.53.5-and-2.2.2-image-pixel-limit-bypass-denial-of-service"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112782", "GHSA-8fxw-crgg-h5h4"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2a5012c6-65d6-3ab7-99ac-28d081be966c", "product": {"name": "grav", "vendor": {"name": "getgrav"}}, "product_version": "1.7.53 <1.7.53.5"}, {"id": "d4adc3ea-9c51-3643-90a0-3e5a111d1631", "product": {"name": "grav", "vendor": {"name": "getgrav"}}, "product_version": "2.0.0-rc.8 <2.2.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "36935209-21c7-368f-93c0-db287630a430", "vendor": {"name": "getgrav"}}], "isExploited": false}